# =============================================================================
# paper/ and presentations/ generated figures
# =============================================================================
# Only track what the document actually embeds, in the ONE format each
# consumes (paper/main.tex wants PDF; presentation.qmd wants SVG, for
# Quarto/reveal.js) -- scripts/make_figures.py's own local convention is
# to always write PDF+SVG together for both --mode paper/presentation,
# so plenty of untracked files accumulate here that were never meant to
# be committed. Add a new `!path` line below whenever a new figure gets
# embedded in main.tex/presentation.qmd; remove one when a figure is
# dropped from the document. A figure under active hand-editing (e.g.
# Inkscape touch-ups) can add its OTHER format here too as a deliberate
# exception -- note why in the commit that adds it.
#
# TODO (deferred, kept as plain SVG for now): these presentation SVGs
# get large -- matplotlib exports every scatter point/CI-band vertex as
# its own full-precision XML path. Fix later: rasterize just the dense
# data layers (ax.scatter(..., rasterized=True), regplot's CI-band
# collection) while keeping text/axes/legends true vector -- smaller
# files, still-crisp labels, no format change needed.
paper/figures/*
!paper/figures/tasks_overview_paper.pdf
!paper/figures/models_overview_paper.pdf
!paper/figures/model_performance.pdf
# lambda_main_edited retired -- the lambda-definition inset that used to
# require hand-placing via Inkscape (see archive'd history/chat) now
# renders NATIVELY inside make_lambda_main itself. lambda_main.pdf/
# sigma_main.pdf/model_performance.pdf above are still each a MANUALLY
# produced file, though -- per instruction, scripts/make_figures.py no
# longer attempts to place any figure's own bold panel labels (A/B/C...)
# itself (repeated automated-placement attempts never got them positioned
# above and to the left of all panel content); the person adds those by
# hand in an SVG editor, using this script's freshly generated {stem}.svg
# (paper/figures/, gitignored, regenerated at will) as the source, and
# exports the result as this same {stem}.pdf. Applies to every current
# and future paper-mode figure with panel labels, not just these three.
!paper/figures/lambda_main.pdf
!paper/figures/sigma_main.pdf
!paper/figures/neural_main.pdf
# neural_main_edited, same hand-touch-up convention as lambda_main_edited
# above -- main.tex now embeds the edited PDF; .svg tracked too as the
# actual hand-edited source for the next round of touch-ups.
!paper/figures/neural_main_edited.pdf
!paper/figures/neural_main_edited.svg
!paper/figures/synaptic_main.pdf
# synaptic_main_edited, same hand-touch-up convention as lambda_main_edited/
# neural_main_edited above -- main.tex now embeds the edited PDF; .svg
# tracked too as the actual hand-edited source for the next round of
# touch-ups.
!paper/figures/synaptic_main_edited.pdf
!paper/figures/synaptic_main_edited.svg
# First supplemental figure (Fig. S1) -- same manually-labeled-PDF
# convention as the main-text figures above.
!paper/figures/lambda_sigma_reliability.pdf
# Second supplemental figure (Fig. S2) -- same convention.
!paper/figures/model_performance_nll.pdf
# Third supplemental figure (Fig. S3) -- single-panel, no A/B/C labels
# needed, but still a manual Inkscape export of the script's own .svg,
# same as every other tracked figure PDF here.
!paper/figures/lambda_balls.pdf

# presentations/figures/ holds BOTH scripts/make_figures.py's --mode
# presentation output (PDF+SVG pairs, only the SVG consumed by
# presentation.qmd/reveal.js) AND every hand-drawn schematic/photo asset
# the deck embeds (consolidated here from the old presentations/images/,
# to avoid two parallel image directories) -- unlike the PDF+SVG pairs,
# those hand-drawn assets have no redundant unconsumed twin format, so a
# per-file whitelist doesn't fit both cases. Ignore only the PDF twins
# (never embedded by Quarto); everything else here is tracked by default.
presentations/figures/*.pdf

# Archive figures (generated; code and docs in archive/ remain tracked)
archive/**/*.png
archive/**/*.pdf
archive/**/*.svg
archive/**/*.jpg
archive/**/*.jpeg
archive/**/*.gif
archive/**/*.eps
archive/**/*.tif
archive/**/*.tiff
archive/**/*.webp

